Subject: [PATCH 06849/11362] ARC round-3 (codex): dc22 honest null, L5 control
 map completed

Continuation of round-3. dc22's L5 wall holds again, but this session
fully grounded the four AA99 quadrant controls precisely ((44,29)=left,
(49,29)=up, (54,29)=right, (59,29)=down on the color-8 structure) and
found a previously-missed hidden control: a large 6 button at (52,48)
teleports the avatar between checker portals, distinct from the L4
checker-tile-click teleport.

Tested all 6/9 phase combinations against the dotted color-15 chute --
it remained non-walkable in every combination, confirming the chute
mechanism is the real remaining unknown. Also found and documented a
genuine soft-lock risk for future attempts: advancing the 2-button cycle
after crossing the row-44 bridge irreversibly traps the avatar (the
final closure is refused because it would delete the avatar's support).

No new level banked; reproducible_total_levels stays 142.

